ip between literature and art has been a long-standing one, with each influencing the other in profound ways. From the ancient Greeks to the present day, the connection between the two has evolved, reflecting the cultural and historical contexts of their time. As we have seen, classic examples of cross-disciplinary cases, such as the poetry of Emily Dickinson influencing the development of American music and the poetry of Langston Hughes influencing the development of jazz music, demonstrate the power of the interdisciplinary dialogue between literature and art. As we move forward, it is essential to continue to explore and celebrate this dialogue, recognizing the ways in which literature and art can enrich and transform each other.", "self_check_notes": ["The essay meets all the constraints, including the use of a historical narrative, classic examples of cross-disciplinary cases, and specific and vivid analysis. The essay also avoids superficial generalizations and focuses on specific examples and case studies."]}, "candidate_retry_note": {"attempts": 1, "validation_errors": []}, "judgment": {"branch_id": "B", "scores_by_criterion": [{"name": "Literary-Visual Arts Integration Analysis", "score_1_to_10": 6, "evidence": "The essay discusses William Blake's integration of poetry and painting but does not provide a deep analysis of how his poetry specifically influences his paintings. It lacks detailed examination of Blake's techniques and thematic connections.", "main_issue": "Insufficient depth in analyzing Blake's specific methods and thematic links between his poetry and paintings."}, {"name": "Cross-Disciplinary Case Studies", "score_1_to_10": 8, "evidence": "The essay includes three cross-disciplinary cases: ancient Greeks, William Blake, and modern examples involving Emily Dickinson and Samuel Barber, as well as Langston Hughes and Duke Ellington. These cases are well-developed and provide specific examples.", "main_issue": "While the cases are well-presented, 