at I had overstepped my bounds. Lord Zhang's face turned red with rage, and Ambassador Li's eyes narrowed into slits.\n\nIn the chaos that followed, a servant stumbled and knocked over a nearby table, shattering a delicate blue-and-white porcelain plate with inlaid gems. The room erupted into a cacophony of noise and confusion. I took advantage of the distraction to slip away, but not before catching a glimpse of a secret token on the floor, partially hidden under the tablecloth. It was a small, intricately carved stone, bearing the symbol of the foreign dignitaries. I knew then that I had stumbled into something much bigger than I had ever imagined.\n\nAs I made my way through the crowded hall, I spotted Master Wang, who nodded discreetly towards a side door. I followed him, and we slipped out into the cool night air. Once we were safely away from prying eyes, Master Wang handed me a small, rolled-up parchment. 'This was on the floor near the entrance,' he whispered. 'I think it might be important.' I unrolled it, and my heart sank. The document hinted at a deep conspiracy, one that threatened the very foundations of our dynasty. I knew then that my life would never be the same.\n\nThe night air was filled with the sweet scent of blooming flowers, but I couldn't shake the feeling of foreboding that had settled in my stomach. I knew that I had to get to the bottom of this conspiracy, but I was just a young scholar from the streets. How could I possibly hope to unravel the threads of a plot that seemed to reach the very highest echelons of power?\n\nI looked over at Master Wang, who was watching me with a serious expression. 'What do we do now?' I asked him. He hesitated, then nodded towards the document. 'We need to get this to someone we can trust. Someone who can help us uncover the truth.' I nodded, determination burning within me. I knew that I had stumbled into a world of politics and intrigue, but I was ready to face whatever lay ahead.\n\nSelf-check notes: Th