's influence on theater extends beyond its themes and characters. The poem's use of language and style has also had a lasting impact on the development of dramatic art. The Iliad's emphasis on poetic language and musicality has influenced the way playwrights and poets approach the art of storytelling.\n\n**Don Quixote: A Bridge Between Literature and Painting**\n\nAnother classic example of literature's influence on other art forms is the 17th-century Spanish novel, Don Quixote. This beloved novel has had a profound impact on the development of oil painting, influencing the work of artists such as Velázquez and Goya. Don Quixote's themes of reality and illusion have inspired artists to explore the relationship between the ideal and the real.\n\nDon Quixote's influence on painting extends beyond its themes and characters. The novel's use of satire and exaggeration has also influenced the way artists approach the representation of reality. The novel's blend of humor and pathos has inspired artists to experiment with new techniques and styles.\n\n**Conclusion: The Significance of Literature in the Fusion of Art Forms**\n\nAs we've seen, literature has played a profound role in the evolution of other art forms. From The Iliad's influence on ancient Greek theater to Don Quixote's impact on oil painting, literature has inspired new styles, techniques, and themes. By exploring the connections between literature and other art forms, we can gain a deeper understanding of the interconnectedness of art and culture.\n\nIn conclusion, literature serves as a bridge between different art forms, inspiring new styles, techniques, and themes. By examining the evolution of literature's influence on other art forms, we can gain a deeper appreciation for the power of literature to shape and transform our understanding of the world around us.\n\nSelf-check notes: This script meets the requirements of the task by including classic examples and background stories, exploring the bridge betw