sing my mind. But I knew what I saw, and I knew what I felt.\n\nThe School of Shadows was a place where the boundaries between reality and madness blurred. It was a place where the rules were constantly shifting, where the past and present collided, and where the living and the dead walked hand in hand.\n\nI knew I had to get out, but the school seemed to have other plans. It was a labyrinth, a maze of corridors and staircases that led nowhere. I was trapped, and I knew I had to find a way out before it was too late.\n\nAs I navigated the ever-changing halls, I stumbled upon a group of students who seemed to be in on a secret. They whispered to each other, their eyes gleaming with a knowing look. I tried to join in, but they pushed me away, their faces twisted in fear.\n\nI realized then that I was not alone in this strange world. There were others like me, others who saw the truth behind the façade. And they were trying to keep it a secret.\n\nI knew I had to find a way to escape, but the school seemed to be shifting and changing around me. I was lost in a world of shadows, a world where the rules were constantly shifting, and the boundaries between reality and madness blurred.\n\nAnd then, I saw her again. The girl in the school uniform, her eyes black as coal, her skin pale as the moon. She stood in the corner of the hallway, watching me with an unblinking gaze.\n\n'Follow the rules,' she said. 'Follow the rules, and you will survive.'\n\nI knew then that I had to follow her, to follow the rules of the School of Shadows. I had to navigate the ever-changing labyrinth, to find a way out before it was too late.\n\nAnd so, I followed her, into the heart of the school, into the depths of madness. I followed her, and I survived.\n\nBut at what cost?\n\nThe School of Shadows was a place where the boundaries between reality and madness blurred. It was a place where the rules were constantly shifting, where the past and present collided, and where the living and the dead 